From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:13:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/h8: Notify the CPUs from _PSR only when the AC
 state changes

_PSR of the AC adapter updates PWRS and calls PNOT, which notifies every
CPU thread with 0x81 (re-evaluate the processor objects), each time the
OS reads the power source and not only on a change: Linux evaluates
_PSR on every read of the online property of the AC power supply, and
other OSes and their drivers poll it.

Call PNOT only when PWRS changes. On a change the notification from
_PSR is still needed: _Q26 and _Q27 call PNOT before the OS evaluates
_PSR, while PWRS can still hold the old state, and on the boards whose
_CST chooses its C-states on PWRS (write_cst_entries() of
cpu/intel/speedstep, as on lenovo/x200) only the later one sees the new
state.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec, with a test SSDT that counts the calls of \_SB.CNOT: PWRS 1
and HPAC 0, the first _PSR returns 0 and calls CNOT, the second returns
0 without calling it; with HPAC 1, _PSR returns 1 and calls it once
more, the next one not; _Q27 notifies AC and calls it, as before. The
DSDTs of lenovo/t60, x200, t420, x230 and t440p build too.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl
index 436fdcfaeb..4477301ec1 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/h8/acpi/ac.asl
@@ -13,11 +13,19 @@ Device(AC)
 	Name(_UID, 0x00)
 	Name(_PCL, Package() { \_SB } )
 
+	/*
+	 * The OS reads _PSR whenever it likes (some poll it): notify the CPUs
+	 * only when PWRS changes. _Q26 and _Q27 notify them too, but before
+	 * the OS gets here to update PWRS, on which some _CST depend.
+	 */
 	Method(_PSR, 0, NotSerialized)
 	{
 		Local0 = HPAC
-		\PWRS = Local0
-		\PNOT()
+		If (\PWRS != Local0)
+		{
+			\PWRS = Local0
+			\PNOT()
+		}
 		return (Local0)
 	}
 
